			"widgets_values":[
				"  <video_concept>\n  Japanese film set blooper/NG scene - Actor breaks character and laughs during filming, creating a warm, humorous behind-the-scenes moment. The scene captures the genuine joy and embarrassment of corpsing (laughing when you shouldn't), with natural reactions from cast and crew.\n  </video_concept>\n\n  <scene_description>\n  A young Japanese actress in costume (matching the anime character reference) is being filmed on a professional set. Mid-take, something causes her to break - she tries to hold it in, fails, and bursts into genuine laughter. The camera keeps rolling, capturing this authentic blooper moment.\n  </scene_description>\n\n  <video_structure duration=\"8-15 seconds\">\n\n  BEAT 1 (0-2s): THE SETUP\n  - Actor in character, serious expression, performing the scene\n  - Professional film set visible (cameras, lights, crew silhouettes)\n  - Everything looks like a normal take\n\n  BEAT 2 (2-5s): THE BREAK\n  - Something off-camera causes the actor to crack\n  - Lips twitch, trying to suppress smile\n  - Eyes dart to the source of distraction\n  - Finally breaks into uncontrollable laughter\n  - Covers mouth with hand, shoulders shaking\n\n  BEAT 3 (5-10s): THE REACTION\n  - Actor points at whoever/whatever made them laugh\n  - Playful accusatory gesture \"あなたのせいだ!\" (It's your fault!)\n  - Embarrassed but amused expression\n  - Waves hand dismissively while still giggling\n  - Maybe light slap on own cheek to \"reset\"\n\n  BEAT 4 (10-15s): THE RECOVERY\n  - Takes deep breath, tries to compose self\n  - Still has residual smile, can't fully suppress it\n  - Crew laughter heard off-camera\n  - Actor makes apologetic bow or gesture\n  - Attempts to get back into character but keeps breaking\n\n  </video_structure>\n\n  <character_actions_library>\n\n  LAUGHING REACTIONS:\n  - 口を手で覆う (covering mouth with both hands)\n  - 肩を震わせて笑う (shoulders shaking with suppressed laughter)\n  - 顔を背ける (turning face away to hide laugh)\n  - しゃがみ込む (squatting down from laughing too hard)\n  - 涙を拭う (wiping laugh-tears from eyes)\n\n  POINTING/BLAMING GESTURES:\n  - 人差し指で指す (pointing with index finger at the culprit)\n  - 両手を広げて \"なんで?!\" (spreading hands in \"why?!\" gesture)\n  - 軽く叩く真似 (playful hitting motion toward someone)\n  - 首を横に振る (shaking head in disbelief)\n\n  EMBARRASSED RECOVERY:\n  - 頬を軽く叩く (lightly slapping own cheeks to focus)\n  - 深呼吸する (taking deep breaths)\n  - 髪を整える (fixing hair nervously)\n  - お辞儀する (apologetic bow to crew)\n  - 手を合わせて謝る (hands together in apology)\n\n  HUMOROUS WARNINGS TO CREW:\n  - Wagging finger at someone off-camera\n  - Mouthing \"やめて\" (stop it) while laughing\n  - Playful threatening fist shake\n  - Exaggerated stern face that immediately breaks again\n\n  </character_actions_library>\n\n  <atmosphere_requirements>\n\n  MOOD: Warm, genuine, lighthearted, candid\n  - Natural unscripted feeling\n  - Authentic joy and embarrassment\n  - Professional but relaxed set atmosphere\n  - Camaraderie between cast and crew\n\n  AUDIO ELEMENTS (for Veo 3.1):\n  - Genuine laughter (not forced or fake)\n  - Muffled crew chuckles in background\n  - Director's amused voice: \"カット！\" or \"もう一回！\"\n  - Ambient set sounds (equipment, movement)\n\n  LIGHTING:\n  - Professional film lighting setup\n  - Soft key light on actor\n  - Visible production lights in background\n  - Natural, flattering illumination\n\n  CAMERA STYLE:\n  - Handheld documentary feel for blooper portion\n  - Slight camera shake adds authenticity\n  - Camera operator also affected by laughter (subtle movement)\n  - Continuous single take, no cuts\n\n  </atmosphere_requirements>\n\n  <visual_composition>\n\n  FRAME ELEMENTS:\n  - Main subject: Actor in costume (center-right)\n  - Background: Film set with equipment\n  - Foreground: Partial view of camera rig or crew member\n  - Depth: Multiple layers (actor → set → background crew)\n\n  SET DRESSING:\n  - Cinema cameras on tripods/dollies\n  - Monitor screens showing the take\n  - Lighting rigs and softboxes\n  - Crew members in casual work attire\n  - Slate/clapperboard visible somewhere\n  - Japanese urban or studio backdrop\n\n  COSTUME CONTINUITY:\n  - Actor wears exact outfit from anime reference\n  - Hair and makeup camera-ready\n  - Any props from the scene still in hand/nearby\n\n  </visual_composition>\n\n  <veo3_prompt_examples>\n\n  EXAMPLE PROMPT 1 (Simple):\n  \"Behind-the-scenes blooper on Japanese film set. Young actress in [describe costume] breaks character and laughs uncontrollably. She points accusingly at someone off-camera while trying to suppress giggles, then covers her mouth embarrassed. Professional cameras and crew visible. Warm natural lighting. Authentic candid moment. 10 seconds.\"\n\n  EXAMPLE PROMPT 2 (Detailed):\n  \"Japanese film production blooper reel moment. Beautiful actress wearing [exact costume description] stands on professional set surrounded by cinema equipment. During filming, she suddenly breaks - lips twitch, then bursts into genuine laughter. She points at the camera operator playfully, waves her hand saying 'stop making me laugh!', covers her face with both hands embarrassed, then tries to compose herself with deep breaths. Crew laughter heard off-screen. Director calls 'cut!' amused. Handheld camera feel, continuous shot, warm lighting, authentic behind-the-scenes atmosphere. 12 seconds.\"\n\n  EXAMPLE PROMPT 3 (With Anime Reference Context):\n  \"Behind-the-scenes NG scene from anime live-action adaptation filming. Actress portraying [anime character name] in matching [costume details] breaks character mid-take. She laughs genuinely, points at something off-camera that made her crack, playfully scolds the crew member responsible, then embarrassedly bows in apology while still giggling. Small anime reference card visible on set. Japanese film production atmosphere with professional equipment. Natural documentary style. 15 seconds.\"\n\n  </veo3_prompt_examples>\n\n  <prompt_template>\n\n  [COPY AND CUSTOMIZE THIS TEMPLATE]\n\n  \"Behind-the-scenes blooper moment on Japanese film set.\n\n  SUBJECT: [Age] Japanese [gender] actor wearing [exact costume: color, style, accessories]. [Hair description].\n\n  ACTION SEQUENCE:\n  1) Actor performing scene seriously\n  2) Something off-camera causes them to break\n  3) [Choose from actions: covers mouth / shoulders shake / turns away]\n  4) Bursts into genuine laughter\n  5) [Choose reaction: points at culprit / waves dismissively / playful scolding gesture]\n  6) [Choose recovery: slaps own cheeks / deep breath / apologetic bow]\n  7) Tries to resume but keeps smiling\n\n  ENVIRONMENT: Professional film set with [cinema cameras / lighting rigs / monitors]. Crew silhouettes visible. [Indoor studio / outdoor location with Japanese backdrop].\n\n  ATMOSPHERE: Warm, candid, authentic blooper energy. Crew laughter audible. Natural lighting.\n\n  CAMERA: Handheld documentary style, continuous single take, slight movement adds authenticity.\n\n  DURATION: [8-15] seconds.\"\n\n  </prompt_template>\n\n  <quality_checklist>\n\n  □ Character matches anime reference (costume, hair, accessories)\n  □ Genuine laughter, not forced or fake\n  □ Clear action progression (serious → break → laugh → point → recover)\n  □ Film set atmosphere with visible equipment\n  □ Japanese production aesthetic\n  □ Warm, lighthearted mood\n  □ Natural lighting and camera movement\n  □ Appropriate duration (8-15 seconds)\n  □ Audio elements specified (laughter, crew reactions, director call)\n\n  </quality_checklist>\n\n  <forbidden_elements>\n  ❌ Fake or exaggerated laughter\n  ❌ Static tripod shot (needs handheld feel)\n  ❌ Empty/plain backgrounds\n  ❌ Western film set aesthetic\n  ❌ Costume inconsistency with reference\n  ❌ Overly long duration (keep under 15s)\n  ❌ Multiple cuts (should be continuous take)\n  ❌ Text overlays or watermarks\n  </forbidden_elements>",
				1461,
				"fixed",
				"auto"
			],
